The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
wq_unregister_lockdep(wq);
```
```c
if (alloc_and_link_pwqs(wq) < 0)
    goto err_unreg_lockdep;
```
```c
wq_init_lockdep(wq);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `wq_unregister_lockdep(wq)` is called unconditionally in the error handling path when `alloc_and_link_pwqs(wq)` fails. If the lockdep key was not registered (i.e., `wq_init_lockdep(wq)` was not called successfully), this leads to a warning from the lockdep core, as it attempts to unregister a key that was never registered.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (wq->lockdep_key_registered)
    wq_unregister_lockdep(wq);
```
```c
wq_free_lockdep(wq);
```
Reason:
The fix involves checking if the lockdep key was registered before calling `wq_unregister_lockdep(wq)`. This prevents the warning from being emitted by ensuring that `wq_unregister_lockdep()` is only called if the key was successfully registered, thus addressing the root cause of the issue.

